From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.security.enterprisedata: the protection policy manager

Windows.Security.EnterpriseData.ProtectionPolicyManager is Windows
Information Protection's policy manager. Office looks it up as it starts
and as it opens files (Excel, OneNote, Outlook: "GetIPolicyProtectionMgr
Statics2 0x80040154" in its log) to learn whether the signed-in identity's
data is protected.

A new module has the class (registered when the prefix is made or
updated), answering as Windows does on a machine where no identity is
managed: IsIdentityManaged and TryApplyProcessUIPolicy false, protection
off (IsProtectionEnabled false, enforcement NoProtection), every access
Allowed, user decryption allowed, nothing revoked, no primary managed
identity; events take a token and are never raised; GetForCurrentView and
IProtectionPolicyManagerInterop::GetForWindow give a manager that keeps
its identity and enterprise indicator; a thread network context closes.
The asynchronous requests are FIXMEs (E_NOTIMPL). Interface layouts and
IIDs are the Windows SDK metadata's; types this module does not use are
spelled IInspectable in its private IDL.

Gate: test/edppolicy-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit: activation, the answers, the
view's manager, a thread context). Mutant SG_MUTANT_EDP_IDENTITY_MANAGED.
Office now logs "IsEDPEnabled false" instead of the class error.
